10856	11050	Minister for finance
Having already been proposed twice to succeed Nicolas Sarkozy as finance minister, Breton was appointed on 24 February 2005 while at France Télécom, replacing Hervé Gaymard.
11051	11131	At the time, he was the country's fourth finance minister within just one year.

11131	11287	During his two and a half years at the head of Bercy, Breton centred his economic policy on the need to reform public finances, specifically to reduce debt.
