11712	11824	He stipulated the maintenance of public deficit below a level of 3% of GDP in 2005 and 2006 as his primary goal.
11825	11946	At the end of 2005 France's deficit fell to 2.9% of its GDP after three consecutive years of surpassing the figure of 3%.
11947	12075	In 2006 the public deficit was further reduced to 2.5% and public debt was recorded to have dramatically fallen to 63.9% of GDP.
12076	12165	For the first time since 1995 the country's budget was in a situation of primary surplus.
12166	12245	At the same time France's GDP rose by 2.1% in 2006 compared with 1.7% in 2005.

